  partName: Heat Shield (2)
  description: The Heat Shield (2) is a tiny, thin-flat component located at the
    top-center-front of the engine, fabricated from Material.004, which provides
    excellent thermal resistance. Its primary function is to protect surrounding
    components from excessive heat generated by the engine, thereby preventing damage
    and ensuring optimal performance. Notably, the heat shield's design allows for
    minimal weight while maintaining maximum thermal protection.
